WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.966
This genie was a giant!

2
00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:19.668
His shiny, bald head touched the ceiling.

3
00:00:19.669 --> 00:00:24.110
A curly, black beard covered half his face.

4
00:00:24.111 --> 00:00:29.789
Muscles bulged on his brown arms, chest, and shoulders.

5
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:35.395
The genie wore black silk pants and big gold earrings.

6
00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:38.448
"Who is this?" cried Zeba.

7
00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:41.305
"Where did he come from?"

8
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:46.186
"He's a genie!" answered Aladdin, leaping to his mother's side.

9
00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:48.375
"He came from the lamp."

10
00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:54.561
"Send him away!" begged Zeba. "I'm afraid."

11
00:00:54.562 --> 00:00:58.650
"I am the genie of the wonderful lamp!"

12
00:00:58.651 --> 00:01:04.450
said the genie, crossing his arms over his huge, bare chest.

13
00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:06.621
"Do not send me away.

14
00:01:06.622 --> 00:01:10.688
I am your slave, ready to serve you."

15
00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:16.093
"I don't want a slave," Zeba said, shaking with fear.

16
00:01:16.094 --> 00:01:17.910
She turned to her son.

17
00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.348
"Tell him to leave, please."

18
00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:25.374
Aladdin snatched the lamp from his mother's hand.

19
00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:29.852
"Do not listen to my mother, genie of the lamp," ordered Aladdin.

20
00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:31.666
"My mother and I are hungry!

21
00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:34.990
Bring us food a sultan would eat!"

22
00:01:34.991 --> 00:01:37.623
The genie disappeared!

23
00:01:37.624 --> 00:01:42.875
But before Aladdin could even blink his eyes, the genie was back.

24
00:01:42.876 --> 00:01:48.452
He carried a large silver tray with six gold plates of food on it.

25
00:01:48.453 --> 00:01:52.046
He put the plates on a carpet on the floor.

26
00:01:52.047 --> 00:01:56.488
"What a feast!" Aladdin shouted.

27
00:01:56.489 --> 00:02:00.068
There was sausage made from beef and lamb.

28
00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:04.820
There was a dish piled high with beet salad and turnips.

29
00:02:04.821 --> 00:02:13.876
Other plates held rice and beans, olives, nuts, and cheese tarts—which smelled so good!

30
00:02:13.877 --> 00:02:18.540
Then—poof—the genie was gone!

31
00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:22.185
"Mother, come!" cried Aladdin with joy.

32
00:02:22.186 --> 00:02:26.527
"Let's enjoy this feast that has been given to us."

33
00:02:26.528 --> 00:02:31.214
"No!" answered Zeba. "I will not eat it.

34
00:02:31.215 --> 00:02:35.209
That terrible genie frightens me!"

35
00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.867
"Sit down here with me,"

36
00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.818
he laughed, patting the carpet next to him.

37
00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:42.369
"Eat and be glad!"

38
00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:48.804
At last, Zeba gave in, sat down, and picked up a cheese tart.

39
00:02:48.805 --> 00:02:53.000
She had never tasted anything like it.

40
00:02:53.001 --> 00:02:59.073
It truly was food for a sultan's table.

41
00:02:59.074 --> 00:03:04.107
"Tell me, son," said Zeba, pouring Aladdin a cup of coffee.

42
00:03:04.108 --> 00:03:08.910
"Was this the genie who freed you from the enchanted treasury?"

43
00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:11.964
"No, no," answered Aladdin.

44
00:03:11.965 --> 00:03:14.497
"The genie of the ring freed me.

45
00:03:14.498 --> 00:03:18.119
He was funny-looking, Mother, and not very tall.

46
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.646
He had bells hanging from his cap."

47
00:03:20.647 --> 00:03:26.349
Aladdin remembered the little, apricot-colored genie and laughed.

48
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:31.529
"The genie of the lamp is a different kind of genie, I think," he added.

49
00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.906
"Yes!" said Aladdin's mother.

50
00:03:34.907 --> 00:03:37.735
"He tried to scare me to death!"

51
00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:41.770
She leaned toward Aladdin and spoke in a whisper,

52
00:03:41.771 --> 00:03:47.337
"Son, you must throw the lamp away—and the ring as well.

53
00:03:47.338 --> 00:03:50.975
They will bring us only trouble!"

54
00:03:50.976 --> 00:03:54.511
"I will not, Mother," said Aladdin.

55
00:03:54.512 --> 00:03:57.160
"We must accept our good fortune.

56
00:03:57.161 --> 00:04:02.120
Think about it—Magrib traveled all this way looking for this lamp.

57
00:04:02.121 --> 00:04:05.954
He wanted only this one thing from the enchanted treasury.

58
00:04:05.955 --> 00:04:10.722
It must be very important, so we will keep the lamp."

59
00:04:10.723 --> 00:04:13.815
"And the ring?" said Zeba.

60
00:04:13.816 --> 00:04:17.114
"The ring too," said Aladdin.

61
00:04:17.115 --> 00:04:21.470
"Without the ring, I would still be buried alive.

62
00:04:21.471 --> 00:04:24.490
You would never have seen me again.

63
00:04:24.491 --> 00:04:28.140
I will never take this ring off my finger."

64
00:04:28.141 --> 00:04:31.430
Aladdin's mother sighed and shook her head.

65
00:04:31.431 --> 00:04:34.818
"Do what you want," she said.

66
00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:42.309
"But I don't want to see that horrible genie again!"
